Previous test only provided a synthetic worldScripts fixture. In THIS test,
OOGFOSWorldScriptsInit created the real read-only enumerable registry,
OOGFOSScriptObjectCreate created an original-style per-script object,
OOGFOSWorldScriptsRegister exposed that same object as worldScripts.ooliteWorld.
The full original upstream oolite-global-prefix.js then enumerated the real
registry into worldScriptNames. The native regression checked that the
enumerated name corresponded to the actual script object and that the script's
real GFOS ship wrapper read bounty=10. Full original Ship.prototype.spawnOne
continues to call native host method and returns 42.

Limitations: Mission/System/Script/Vector3D etc. are STILL TEST FIXTURE
constructors, NOT the full original OOJS* class ports. Ship is an actual GFOS
host wrapper but only a controlled native fixture, not the complete Oolite
Universe/ShipEntity. The original game remains unplayable at this gate.
